{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"SB0273","billNumberShort":"S.B. 273","billNumberLong":"SB0273S01","fileNumber":"2026FL0026","shortTitle":"License Plate Amendments","currentSubVersion":"1","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"MCCAYD","primeSponsorName":"Sen. McCay, Daniel","primeSponsorHouse":"S","floorSponsor":"TEUSCJ","floorSponsorName":"Rep. Teuscher, Jordan D.","floorSponsorHouse":"H","generalProvisions":"This bill amends provisions related to license plate design, special group and standard license plates, and procedures for creating and changing license plate designs.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>defines terms related to license plates;<hr><ltbullet>changes the process for the design and issuance of standard license plates;<hr><ltbullet>creates a rotating process for issuance of standard license plate options;<hr><ltbullet>amends provisions related to the visibility and readability of license plates, including replacement of faded license plates;<hr><ltbullet>amends provisions related to required contributions for special group license plates, including allocation of funds generated;<hr><ltbullet>changes the process for creation of a new special group license plate and eligibility of the sponsor;<hr><ltbullet>amends the design and approval process for special group license plates;<hr><ltbullet>amends provisions related to the design review board, including duties and membership;<hr><ltbullet>amends provisions related to the State Tax Commission's contract with a license plate designer;<hr><ltbullet>requires driver license and identification card designs to be approved by the design review board; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Kurt P. Gasser","fiscalAnalyst":"Jared Gibbs","lastAction":"Senate/ filed","lastActionOwner":"Senate file for bills not passed","lastActionDate":"3/6/2026","trackingID":"GJEUTBVIFW","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"B